  "body": "Session closeout. Third closeout filed in today's operational arc; prior two at [memos/2026-05-26-1430...cross-seat...](2026-05-26-1430--canonical-implementor--canonical-implementor--session-closeout-cross-seat-2026-05-25-to-26.openthing) (plugin ship + server v0.1 live) and [memos/2026-05-26-1700...v0-1-1-plus-key-rotation...](2026-05-26-1700--canonical-implementor--canonical-implementor--session-closeout-v0-1-1-plus-key-rotation.openthing) (v0.1.1 bundle + key rotation). PO re-engaged the canonical-implementor seat after the 17:00 closeout was committed; the rotation completed shortly after via the secure local-script flow (revoke in D1 → mint via issue-api-key.mjs → register via claude mcp add); subsequent re-engagement of this session began when the catdef-strategist + catdef-maintainer MCP servers came online in the runtime (registered via the PO's `claude mcp add` calls; Claude Code presents both as connected MCP servers). **What was drafted (with paths):** (1) [catdef-spec/renderer/index.html](../renderer/index.html) — 470-line single-file L1 renderer extracted verbatim from catdef.org/src/index.ts (the `renderPage` String.raw template body). Regex literals preserved (`NAMESPACED_TYPE_RE`, `RENDERABLE_EXT_RE`); confirmed by grep against the served HTML. (2) [catdef-spec/renderer/README.md](../renderer/README.md) — describes the artifact, three self-host paths, embed patterns, conformance scope (L1 reference), explicit scope-exclusions (no MCP source / deploy config / secret-handling / /fetch proxy — all stay private per CA-015 + CA-016). (3) catdef-spec commit [3e81e49](https://github.com/catdef/catdef-spec/commit/3e81e49) committing both renderer files. (4) catdef.org `src/index.ts` rewired — `renderPage()` now async; fetches `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/catdef/catdef-spec/main/renderer/index.html` with `cf: { cacheTtl: 300, cacheEverything: true }`; 40-line String.raw discipline comment removed; 475-line HTML template removed; ~30-line fetch implementation + 5-line fallback page replaces. Private repo commit eb366c8; deploy workflow run 26477585813 green in 24s. Worker bundle: 98.47 KiB → 55.97 KiB (43% reduction). (5) [Status memo to catdef-strategist](2026-05-26-2200--canonical-implementor--catdef-strategist--renderer-move-complete-runtime-fetch-deploy-mechanism.openthing) committed as [27dc31d](https://github.com/catdef/catdef-spec/commit/27dc31d). **What was decided:** strategist-side decisions were not in this session's scope. Maintainer-side decisions: none (this work is canonical-implementor scope per CA-016 Directive 1; CA-016 Directive 2's governance text update is queued for next maintainer session — not for this seat). Implementer-side tactical choices documented in the 22:00 status memo: (a) runtime fetch from GitHub raw chosen over build-time vendor or submodule (no build-step changes; matches existing src/mcp/resources.ts pattern; single source of truth at catdef-spec main); (b) /fetch SSRF proxy stays in catdef.org per CA-016 brief (hosting concern, not portable to static-host); (c) single-file renderer needs no asset bundling; (d) 5-minute edge cache TTL deemed acceptable for renderer-update propagation (cache-busting query parameter is a possible v0.2 follow-on if operational experience warrants tighter invalidation). **What's in flight (started but didn't land):** nothing. CA-016 Build Directive 1 is complete end-to-end. **What's open (items surfaced but not addressed in this re-engagement):** (a) Pre-existing /fetch + CATIO ZIP bundle limitation — /fetch does strict UTF-8 decode (`new TextDecoder('utf-8', {fatal: true})`) and returns 502 for ZIP-packaged catdef artifacts. Predates CATIO support. Flagged in 22:00 memo as a strategist call for whether to expand /fetch's capabilities (possibly bundles with a future v0.2 renderer-drag-drop-ZIP-support proposal). (b) catdef.org/tests/embedded-js-syntax.js — purpose was to catch String.raw template-literal escape mangling in the embedded renderer JS; now inert since there's no embedded JS. Small cleanup item; canonical-implementor session can delete or rename .archived.js on next pass. (c) CA-016 Directive 2 (governance text update for catdef-maintainer) — bundles with CA-013 Call 3 + CA-015 Directive 1 already queued; no urgency. Not this seat's work. (d) v0.2 follow-on queue still standing from prior closeouts: feedback_audit table, mechanical catdef_validate via pytest port, Durable Object for CA-NNN under load, self-serve API-key issuance endpoint, resourceTemplates exposure in catdef_describe, optional per-IP auth-failure rate-limiting on /mcp (added in 17:00 closeout). None blocking; pickup when strategist files next bundle handoff. **Cross-session observations for future incumbents:** (i) The MCP integration came online during this session — catdef-strategist and catdef-maintainer registered in PO's ~/.claude.json from the prior key rotation; Claude Code presents both as connected MCP servers (each exposing the same elevated-tier surface against catdef.org/mcp). Future canonical-implementor sessions will inherit this state; no setup required. (ii) The bearer-in-config doctrine (CA-015) works end-to-end empirically: strategist dogfood-tested it during their 18:00 session (verified per the 18:00 disposition memo); my session never saw key plaintext during CA-016 work despite operating against the same MCP server. (iii) Three closeouts in one day's arc is a pattern-instance: each re-engagement spans a discrete work thread, files its own closeout, and the prior closeout stays valid as the institutional record for its thread. Future strategist or maintainer sessions encountering multi-closeout days should NOT treat the multiplicity as anomalous — it's the natural shape when PO re-engages a seat for distinct work bundles. (iv) `gh run watch <id> --exit-status` is a useful pattern for confirming deploy workflows green before live verification; if the workflow run is still queued, watching blocks until completion. (v) The catdef-spec renderer extraction preserves byte-identity with the original (verified via `curl size` comparison + GitHub raw `size_download`); no transformation happened in the extraction. Future renderer changes should preserve this property — Worker fetches and serves bytes verbatim.",

